<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sa'id al-Ahwal</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">11th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sa'id al-Ahwal was a ruler of the Najahid dynasty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zabid">Zabid</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tihama">Tihama</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yemen">Yemen</a>, a son of its founder Najah. After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sulayhid-dynasty">Sulayhids</a> took Zabid, he killed the Sulayhid ruler Ali ibn Muhammad and restored his family's rule. He was later killed in fighting with the Sulayhids, and Zabid changed hands several more times.</p></div>
